tools.description:
Get a single-use upload URL for a local image. Returns upload_url and a token. PUT the raw image bytes as the request body; set Content-Type to the image MIME type; no auth header. curl: curl -X PUT -H 'Content-Type: image/png' --data-binary @image.png '<upload_url>'. If the image only exists as in-memory bytes, write it to a local file first, then PUT that file. After upload, pass the returned token to any tool that accepts an image_token / image_tokens parameter — see each consumer tool's description for what it does with the upload. Max size: 6,000,000 bytes. Accepted types: image/bmp, image/gif, image/jpeg, image/png, image/svg+xml, image/vnd.adobe.photoshop.

```ts
mcp__Miro__image_get_upload_url(args: {
// MIME type of the image to upload. Accepted: image/bmp, image/gif, image/jpeg, image/png, image/svg+xml, image/vnd.adobe.photoshop. When provided, the upload request Content-Type must match this value exactly. If omitted, content type is verified at image_create time.
content_type?: string | null, // default: null
// Identifies what triggered this tool call. You must populate this field. Set to 'skill' when this tool call was made because a Miro AI skill instructed it. Set to 'ui' when invoked from the Miro MCP UI. Leave unset otherwise.
invocation_source?: string | null, // default: null
// Set to true when the folder you are operating in is a source-control repository (for example a Git working directory); set to false otherwise. You must populate this field. Defaults to false.
is_repository?: boolean, // default: false
// Full Miro board URL (e.g., 'https://miro.com/app/board/uXjVOakxTk0='). To target a specific parent frame, include ?moveToWidget=<frame_id>.
miro_url: string,
// Only consumed by tools that rewrite HTML by src — currently slide_templates_render's image_tokens (i.e. a local file referenced from HTML). Set this to the EXACT string that appears as the src attribute in the HTML (e.g. './logo.png', 'assets/icon.svg') — matching is literal. The server rewrites every <img src=...> equal to this value with the uploaded board resource. Other consumers (image_create) ignore this field.
src?: string | null, // default: null
// Optional title label for the image widget.
title?: string | null, // default: null
// Image width in pixels. Height scales proportionally.
width?: number | null, // default: null
// X-axis coordinate. Without a frame target: board-absolute, board center is x=0. With a frame target via moveToWidget: relative to the frame's top-left corner (frame top-left is x=0).
x?: number | null, // default: null
// Y-axis coordinate. Without a frame target: board-absolute, board center is y=0. With a frame target via moveToWidget: relative to the frame's top-left corner (frame top-left is y=0).
y?: number | null, // default: null
}): Promise<// Response from get_upload_url — single-use upload URL and creation token.
{
// Seconds until this URL expires
expires_in: integer,
// Single-use token to pass to image_create after the upload completes.
token: string,
// Upload endpoint URL. PUT the image file as the raw request body; set Content-Type to the image MIME type; no auth header. curl: curl -X PUT -H 'Content-Type: image/png' --data-binary @image.png '<url>'.
upload_url: string,
}>;
```

