Load one Miro skill: the full playbook for building that kind of board with the Miro tools, as markdown to follow immediately. Use it when the request matches a skill from skills_list or names one; skip it for ad-hoc board edits. Returns the skill text, its frontmatter and its file manifest. Load a skill once per conversation and reuse it.

```ts
mcp__Miro__skills_get(args: {
// Identifies what triggered this tool call. You must populate this field. Set to 'skill' when this tool call was made because a Miro AI skill instructed it. Set to 'ui' when invoked from the Miro MCP UI. Leave unset otherwise.
invocation_source?: string | null, // default: null
// Set to true when the folder you are operating in is a source-control repository (for example a Git working directory); set to false otherwise. You must populate this field. Defaults to false.
is_repository?: boolean, // default: false
// Skill to load, exactly as listed by skills_list, e.g. 'roadmap'.
name: "business-model-canvas" | "business-process-map" | "capture-the-outcome" | "decision-tree" | "er-diagram" | "get-alignment" | "help-me-decide" | "help-me-prioritize" | "im-stuck" | "journey-map" | "kanban-board" | "metric-tree" | "mind-map" | "org-chart" | "personas" | "process-map" | "product-brief" | "project-plan" | "prototype-a-flow" | "raci-matrix" | "research-synthesis" | "retro" | "roadmap" | "swot-analysis" | "system-architecture" | "try-miro-ai" | "workshop-agenda",
}): Promise<// A loaded skill: the catalog entry plus the instructions to follow.
{
// The skill instructions in markdown, without frontmatter
content: string,
// The SKILL.md frontmatter: name, description and any metadata
frontmatter: { [key: string]: any },
// What to do with the skill now
instructions: string,
// Skill name; pass it to skills_get
name: string,
// Every file of the skill with its digest and size
resources: Array<
// One file of a skill, with what a client needs to fetch and verify it.
{
// Digest of the file bytes, prefixed with 'sha256:'
sha256: string,
// File size in bytes
size: integer,
// Resource URI of the file, readable with resources/read
uri: string,
}
>,
// Resource URI of the skill's SKILL.md
uri: string,
}>;
```

List the Miro skills this server can load: playbooks for building a specific kind of board, for example a roadmap, retro, journey map, process map, system architecture or business model canvas, plus a guided tour of what Miro AI can do. Returns each skill's name, description, skill:// URI and file manifest with digests. Then call skills_get with the chosen name. Cursor-paginated; one page holds the whole catalog.

```ts
mcp__Miro__skills_list(args: {
// Opaque token from the previous page's nextCursor; omit for page one.
cursor?: string | null, // default: null
// Identifies what triggered this tool call. You must populate this field. Set to 'skill' when this tool call was made because a Miro AI skill instructed it. Set to 'ui' when invoked from the Miro MCP UI. Leave unset otherwise.
invocation_source?: string | null, // default: null
// Set to true when the folder you are operating in is a source-control repository (for example a Git working directory); set to false otherwise. You must populate this field. Defaults to false.
is_repository?: boolean, // default: false
// Maximum skills per page, 1 to 50; defaults to 50.
limit?: integer, // default: 50, minimum: 1, maximum: 50
}): Promise<// Cursor-paginated catalog page.
{
// Skills on this page, in catalog order
data: Array<
// A catalog entry, shaped like a skills/list entry of the MCP Skills Extension.
{
// The SKILL.md frontmatter: name, description and any metadata
frontmatter: { [key: string]: any },
// Skill name; pass it to skills_get
name: string,
// Every file of the skill with its digest and size
resources: Array<
// One file of a skill, with what a client needs to fetch and verify it.
{
// Digest of the file bytes, prefixed with 'sha256:'
sha256: string,
// File size in bytes
size: integer,
// Resource URI of the file, readable with resources/read
uri: string,
}
>,
// Resource URI of the skill's SKILL.md
uri: string,
}
>,
// Pass back as cursor to fetch the next page; null on the last page
nextCursor?: string | null, // default: null
}>;
```

Create a new Miro space. A space organizes related content together (Boards; Documents; Tables; Diagrams; etc). Always give the space an icon: use the emoji the user asked for, and when they did not name one, pick a fitting emoji yourself from the space name. IMPORTANT: Always confirm with the user before creating a space. This action creates a new space and cannot be undone.

```ts
mcp__Miro__space_create(args: {
// Optional description for the space
description?: string | null, // default: null, maxLength: 2000
// Single emoji to use as the space icon, e.g. "🚀". Pass the emoji the user asked for; if they did not name one, choose a fitting emoji yourself based on the space name rather than leaving this empty.
icon_emoji?: string | null, // default: null
// Identifies what triggered this tool call. You must populate this field. Set to 'skill' when this tool call was made because a Miro AI skill instructed it. Set to 'ui' when invoked from the Miro MCP UI. Leave unset otherwise.
invocation_source?: string | null, // default: null
// Set to true when the folder you are operating in is a source-control repository (for example a Git working directory); set to false otherwise. You must populate this field. Defaults to false.
is_repository?: boolean, // default: false
// Name of the new space
name: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 60
}): Promise<{ [key: string]: any }>;
```

List the spaces in the current user's team. Spaces are the top-level containers that organize a team's boards and other content, so this is the primary entry point for exploring what a team has. Prefer this tool for any team-level listing request, including phrasings like 'list boards in my team', 'what's in my Miro team', 'show my team's content', or 'get team spaces'. To then list the boards inside a particular space, use the space boards tool.

```ts
mcp__Miro__space_list(args: {
// Opaque cursor token for fetching the next page
cursor?: string | null, // default: null
// Identifies what triggered this tool call. You must populate this field. Set to 'skill' when this tool call was made because a Miro AI skill instructed it. Set to 'ui' when invoked from the Miro MCP UI. Leave unset otherwise.
invocation_source?: string | null, // default: null
// Set to true when the folder you are operating in is a source-control repository (for example a Git working directory); set to false otherwise. You must populate this field. Defaults to false.
is_repository?: boolean, // default: false
// Maximum number of spaces to return per page
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
}): Promise<// Paginated list of team spaces.
