Get the history of a row's Latest Update field. The Latest Update field accumulates the text updates submitted for that row over time; this returns those entries ordered chronologically. Provide the table via its Miro URL and the target row via rowId. 

Response includes for each entry: text, author_id (Miro user ID of the author), created_at and modified_at (ISO 8601 timestamps), plus the total number of entries.

```ts
mcp__Miro__table_get_latest_update_history(args: {
// Identifies what triggered this tool call. You must populate this field. Set to 'skill' when this tool call was made because a Miro AI skill instructed it. Set to 'ui' when invoked from the Miro MCP UI. Leave unset otherwise.
invocation_source?: string | null, // default: null
// Set to true when the folder you are operating in is a source-control repository (for example a Git working directory); set to false otherwise. You must populate this field. Defaults to false.
is_repository?: boolean, // default: false
// Full Miro URL to a specific item (e.g., 'https://miro.com/app/board/uXjVOakxTk0=/?moveToWidget=3458764516062720430'). Must include moveToWidget or focusWidget query parameter.
miro_url: string, // minLength: 1
// Stable identifier of the row whose Latest Update field history to fetch.
row_id: string, // pattern: /^[0-9a-zA-Z_-]{1,64}$/
}): Promise<// Response from get_latest_update_history tool.
{
// Entries from the row's Latest Update field history, ordered chronologically
entries: Array<
// A single entry in a Latest Update field's history.
{
// Miro user ID of the author of this update. May be null when the author is unknown (e.g. system-generated or anonymous updates).
author_id?: string | null, // default: null
// ISO 8601 timestamp when this update was first created
created_at?: string | null, // default: null
// ISO 8601 timestamp when this update was last modified
modified_at?: string | null, // default: null
// Text content of this update
text?: string | null, // default: null
}
>,
// Full Miro URL to the table
miro_url: string,
// Total number of entries in the Latest Update field history
total: integer,
}>;
```

Search for people in the current user's organization and return their name, email, and user id. Scoped automatically to the caller's organization and team. Use this to resolve a person the user names or describes (for example before sharing a board or mentioning someone). The query matches against user names; an email address or its prefix may also match, but exact email lookup is not guaranteed. Returns the closest matches ordered by relevance, or an empty list when nobody matches.

```ts
