Manage jobs on a monday platform agent.
Jobs define WHAT work runs and own one or more triggers that define WHEN it runs.

ACTIONS:
- list:   { action:"list", agent_id } — returns jobs, their instructions, stable ids, and nested triggers.
- create: { action:"create", agent_id, name?, instructions?, enabled?, triggers?, model?, thinking_level? }
- update: { action:"update", agent_id, job_id, name?, instructions?, enabled?, triggers?, remove_trigger_ids?, model?, thinking_level? }
- delete: { action:"delete", agent_id, job_id } — removes the job and all nested triggers.
- run:    { action:"run", agent_id, job_id } — runs the job once now, regardless of its triggers.

RULES:
- Agent-level Identity, tone, and guardrails belong in manage_agent. Job-specific work belongs here.
- Call agent_catalog action:"list_triggers" before adding a trigger. Never guess block_reference_id.
- trigger_id is the stable CRUD identity. node_id is only the workflow position.
- Updates are patches: omitted jobs and triggers remain unchanged.
- Credentialed third-party triggers cannot be configured here. Complete those trigger connections in monday.com.
- action:"run" is fire-and-forget: a returned trigger_uuid means the run was accepted, not finished.
- A job listed with from_template:true comes from the agent's template. It can be run, and its update only adds triggers (no trigger_id) or removes the agent's own (remove_trigger_ids); it cannot be deleted.
- Job creation and trigger registration are not atomic with agent creation.
  If this tool fails after manage_agent created an agent, keep the agent and retry this tool.

RELATED TOOLS:
- manage_agent — create the agent and configure its agent-level Identity
- agent_catalog — discover supported trigger types and required fields
- manage_agent_triggers — legacy flat-trigger compatibility

```ts
mcp__monday_com__manage_agent_jobs(args: {
// "list" — inspect jobs and nested triggers. "create" — create a job. "update" — patch a job and its triggers. "delete" — remove a job and all nested triggers. "run" — run a job once now.
action: "list" | "create" | "update" | "delete" | "run",
agent_id: string, // minLength: 1
// Used with create/update. Whether this job is enabled.
enabled?: boolean,
// Used with create/update. Job-specific instructions followed whenever this job runs.
instructions?: string, // minLength: 1
// Required for update/delete/run. Stable job UUID returned by list/create.
job_id?: string, // minLength: 1
// Used with create/update. Omit unless the user asks for a model for this job: the job then runs on the agent's model. A catalog model id pins one, "auto" lets the platform choose, and "agent_default" removes the job's own model on update.
model?: "auto" | "agent_default" | "claude-sonnet" | "claude-sonnet-5" | "claude-sonnet-5-5" | "claude-opus" | "claude-opus-5" | "claude-opus-5-5" | "claude-haiku-5-5" | "claude-fable-5" | "gpt-6.2-astra" | "gpt-6-astra" | "gpt-6.2-sol" | "gpt-6.1-sol" | "gpt-6.1-terra" | "gpt-6-sol" | "gpt-6-luna" | "gpt-5.6-sol" | "gpt-5.6-terra" | "gpt-5.6-luna" | "gpt-5.2" | "gemini-4-neon" | "gemini-4-hydrogen" | "gemini-4-carbon" | "gemini-4-argon" | "gemini-3.8-flash" | "gemini-3.7-flash" | "gemini-3.5-flash-lite" | "gemini-2.5-flash" | "grok-4.7" | "nemotron-3-nano",
// Used with create/update. Display name of the job.
name?: string, // minLength: 1
