Set up, configure, or design a CRM of any kind (sales pipeline, clients, leads, deals, contacts, accounts) in monday.com, including a bare "set up a CRM" request or a question about which CRM setup fits a business. Propose a CRM board layout for a monday.com account — which boards to create, their purpose, pipeline stages, and tracked field areas — in the user's own vocabulary. Covers setting up, configuring, or restructuring a CRM of any kind: sales pipelines, client, lead, or deal tracking, industry CRMs such as real estate, recruiting, agency, or fundraising, and the structure of a CRM used elsewhere such as HubSpot or Salesforce. Also answers which CRM setup fits a business. Read-only: does not create or modify boards, items, or columns; `build-crm-setup` does that after the user has seen the proposal and approved it in a later message.

Works from no context at all: a bare "set up a CRM" is enough to start. The tool runs its own short interview and designs the whole board set, so no clarifying questions beforehand and no board-by-board assembly with individual board tools are needed. Does not compare CRM vendors: "what is the best CRM?" is a product question, not a setup request, and a tailored setup can follow once the user wants one. Does not find or source new leads.

Returns `NEEDS_INFO` with exactly one targeted question when the context is too thin for a useful proposal, the expected first result for a bare request; caps at three questions per conversation. Returns `PROPOSAL` with a board list and a `setup_token` once there is enough context, plus `warnings` for defaults used in place of missing answers and for common setup mistakes. To change a proposal the user has seen, call it again with its `setup_token` and `refinements`. A `setup_token` that expired within the last week still carries the answers, and the plan is regenerated for approval. Returns `INVALID_TOKEN`, without a token, when the supplied `setup_token` cannot be used; omit it to restart. Returns `CRM_REQUIRED` when monday CRM is not enabled on the account.

Scope: this tool builds CRM structure only. It does not import records from another CRM, build pure project-delivery workflows, model nested client-of-client accounts, split one motion into product or regional pipelines, enforce per-assignee privacy, or undo created boards. Saved views, automations, and mirror columns are not created by this version. Phone-first and field-sales teams can use the boards but should skip the optional email connection. Email and calendar consent must be completed by the user in a browser. Importing contacts from Gmail into the Contacts board is optional, offered after the boards are built, and happens only if the user agrees to it. Use individual board tools or a manual setup for pure project delivery and nested client-account structures.

