Creates a new Vibe app from a natural-language prompt. Returns immediately with app_id and editor_link — the URL of the Vibe builder/chat page for the new app (https://{accountSlug}.monday.com/vibe/app/{appId}); the user can open it right away to watch generation in progress. Generation itself runs asynchronously — poll vibe_get for status. Optional: workspace_id to create the app in a specific workspace, board_ids to connect existing boards (omit to auto-create), view_id to host a dashboard widget, and model when the user asks for a specific model. Generation runs on monday's AI infrastructure; the account admin may block AI vendors. Pass wait_seconds to wait up to that long for the build, with progress updates while it runs; the response then adds turn_status: IDLE = the build finished, with summary (the build's final message) and suggestions (follow-up prompts, when there are any), so there is no need to call vibe_get for them; BUSY = still building, call vibe_get with wait_seconds again (if supported) or check later; AWAITING_ANSWER = the build waits on the user. With pending_question: show the user each question with its options, marking the recommended ones, and send the answers with its card_id to vibe_answer; a question already answered carries its selected options or skipped: true, and needs no new answer; questions left unanswered after auto_answer_in_seconds are answered with the recommended options and the build goes on. With pending_approval: an action needs the user's approval, which only the editor can give; tell the user to open editor_link. With neither: tell the user to open editor_link. A new vibe_update instead drops the pending question or action and starts a new build. A response without turn_status did not wait.

