Fetch a Vibe app by id. App metadata is always returned, including editor_link — the URL of the Vibe builder/chat page for this app (https://{accountSlug}.monday.com/vibe/app/{appId}); usable as soon as the app row exists. Pass `include` to add expensive slices: status (refreshes status + adds is_busy, default true), messages (with optional from_date), code (generated files — the current version unless version_id or version_status is given), code_versions. With status, an app that is not busy may still have a build waiting on the user: pending_question is then added (answer it with vibe_answer; unanswered questions get their recommended options after auto_answer_in_seconds), or pending_approval (the user approves it at editor_link). Pass wait_seconds to wait up to that long for the build, with progress updates while it runs; the response then adds turn_status: IDLE = the build finished, with summary (the build's final message) and suggestions (follow-up prompts, when there are any), so there is no need to call vibe_get for them; BUSY = still building, call vibe_get with wait_seconds again (if supported) or check later; AWAITING_ANSWER = the build waits on the user. With pending_question: show the user each question with its options, marking the recommended ones, and send the answers with its card_id to vibe_answer; a question already answered carries its selected options or skipped: true, and needs no new answer; questions left unanswered after auto_answer_in_seconds are answered with the recommended options and the build goes on. With pending_approval: an action needs the user's approval, which only the editor can give; tell the user to open editor_link. With neither: tell the user to open editor_link. A new vibe_update instead drops the pending question or action and starts a new build. A response without turn_status did not wait.

