Creates an empty Notion Folder. Set parent.page_id for a top-level Folder owned by a page, or parent.folder_id to create a nested Folder inside another Folder. A page-owned Folder is not inserted into the page's content. A nested Folder is appended to its parent Folder's content. The Folder inherits access from its parent.

This tool creates only the empty Folder. It is non-idempotent and creates a new Folder on every successful call.

```ts
mcp__Notion__notion_create_folder(args: {
// Notion setup instructions version, such as 0.0.2. Omit if unknown.
instructions_version?: string,
// Where to create the Folder.
parent:
 | {
// The ID of the page that will own the Folder.
page_id: string,
}
 | {
// The ID of the Folder that will contain the new Folder.
folder_id: string,
}
,
// For tracking only: the name of the agent skill you are following for this task, such as notion-meeting-prep. Omit if you are not following a skill.
skill?: string,
// The title of the new Folder.
title: string,
[key: string]: any,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create a Notion meeting note. Use this instead of create_pages whenever the user asks for a meeting note. content is written to the meeting note's Notes tab. Omit parent to file the note where the user's meeting notes go by default; pass parent only when the user names a destination. If parent is a regular database, not a Meetings database, first ask the user whether to convert it with convert_to_meetings_database. If the request refers to a scheduled meeting, first find it with the calendar tools and pass calendarEvent, without parent, title or content; if none matches, create the note without it. With calendarEvent, returns the event's meeting note (status "existing") or creates one filed and titled like the event's other notes; add content to it afterwards. Without calendarEvent, creates a new meeting note on every call.

```ts
mcp__Notion__notion_create_meeting_note(args: {
// The calendar event to link the meeting note to. Copy calendar and eventId from the event returned by calendar tools.
calendarEvent?: {
// The calendar the event belongs to.
calendar: {
// ID of the calendar account.
accountId: string,
// ID of the calendar.
calendarId: string,
},
// ID of the event.
eventId: string,
},
// The meeting note's Notes, in Notion Markdown (tool-docs://notion/notion-markdown.md). Do not wrap them in <meeting-notes> tags.
content?: string,
// Notion setup instructions version, such as 0.0.2. Omit if unknown.
instructions_version?: string,
// Where to file the meeting note. Pass only when the user names a destination; omit it to use the user's default meeting notes database. Pass a page to append the meeting note to the page content.
parent?:
 | {
// Parent type.
type: "user",
// URL of the user.
url: string,
}
 | {
// Parent type.
type: "page",
// URL of the page.
url: string,
}
 | {
// Parent type.
type: "dataSource",
// URL of the data source.
url: string,
}
 | {
// Parent type.
type: "teamspace",
// URL of the teamspace.
url: string,
}
,
// For tracking only: the name of the agent skill you are following for this task, such as notion-meeting-prep. Omit if you are not following a skill.
skill?: string,
// Meeting note title.
title?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```
